# Responsive UI

Designs are **mobile-first**. A layout that only works at desktop width is unfinished.

## Breakpoints (Tailwind)

| Prefix | Min width | Use for |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| (none) | ~360px | Default. Must be usable. |
| `sm:` | 640px | Two-column stats, extra meta |
| `md:` | 768px | Optional denser toolbars |
| `lg:` | 1024px | Sidebar rail, split panes, charts |

## Must

- Grids collapse: `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4`
- Text and rows wrap: `min-w-0`, `flex-wrap`, `truncate` / `break-words`
- Horizontal scroll only inside a named region (tables: `brm-table-scroll`)
- Skeletons use `%` / `max-w-full` / `w-3/4` — never a fixed `w-64` that overflows a phone
- Page loads use the matching skeleton in `LoadingSpinner.tsx`, not a spinner
- Test at ~360px and at `lg` before shipping a screen

## Must not

- Fixed pixel widths on page chrome (`w-[900px]`, `min-w-[40rem]` on the page)
- Physical `left`/`right` for layout — use `ps`/`pe`/`ms`/`me` (RTL)
- Hide the only way to complete a task on small screens
